OL,3,AChildren among 109 dead after boat
OL,4,Acapsizes off Djibouti, UN says
OL,5,
OL,6,FAt least 109 migrants including 15
OL,7,Fchildren have died and dozens more are
OL,8,Fstill missing after a boat sank off the
OL,9,Fcoast of Djibouti, the International
OL,10,FOrganization for Migration (IOM) has
OL,11,Fsaid.
OL,13,FThe boat was travelling from Djibouti
OL,14,Fto Yemen with 350 people on board, when
OL,15,Fit capsized near the port town of Obock
OL,16,Fon Thursday night. Around 80 people
OL,17,Fwere rescued, the IOM said.
OL,19,FIOM's Djibouti mission chief Alexandre
OL,20,FCoissac called the tragedy a "stark
OL,21,Freminder" of the dangers migrants face
OL,22,Fwhile seeking a new life elsewhere.
OL,23,APub: 11-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB Nat NewsC Nat TVF Clean Feed
